<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">16 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 16 October, from 690 to 1946.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/wu-zetian" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wu-zetian.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">690 <span class="tih-ago">1,336 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wu Zetian proclaims herself emperor of China</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Wu Zetian, long the power behind the Tang throne, took the title of emperor and founded her own Zhou dynasty. She remains the only woman to rule China in her own name, and expanded recruitment by examination.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wu-zetian">Wu Zetian</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/paris" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paris.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1793 <span class="tih-ago">233 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Marie Antoinette is guillotined in Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a two-day trial before the Revolutionary Tribunal, the former queen Marie Antoinette was executed on the Place de la Révolution. She was 37, and her husband Louis XVI had been executed nine months earlier.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-world-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1813 <span class="tih-ago">213 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Battle of Leipzig begins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Austrian, Prussian, Russian and Swedish armies attacked Napoleon around Leipzig. With some 600,000 soldiers engaged over three days, the 'Battle of the Nations' was the largest in Europe before the First World War.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1916 <span class="tih-ago">110 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Margaret Sanger opens the first US birth control clinic</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Margaret Sanger, her sister and a colleague opened a birth control clinic in Brownsville, Brooklyn. Police closed it nine days later, but Sanger's campaign led to the organisation that became Planned Parenthood.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/nuremberg" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nuremberg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1946 <span class="tih-ago">80 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ten Nazi leaders are hanged at Nuremberg</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Ten men sentenced by the International Military Tribunal, including Ribbentrop, Keitel and Streicher, were hanged in Nuremberg prison's gymnasium. Göring had taken poison the night before.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuremberg">Nuremberg</a></div></div></li></ol>
